# Explore the data

<details class="ex-about">
<summary>About the explorer</summary>

Choose a question and a characteristic to compare by, such as age or gender, and narrow the data down to certain surveys or ages if you like. Because the surveys differ in age range, recruitment and timing, each survey is shown in its own panel unless you pool them, and pooled differences may partly reflect who took part in each survey.

The address of the page changes with your choices, so you can share a link to any chart. All calculations run in your browser, on the data described on the [data page](data.qmd).

</details>
:::

